.TH RGBDNS-LOG-REPORT 1 "August 2026" "rgbdns 0.5.1"
.SH NAME
rgbdns-log-report \- aggregate rgbdns query logs by authoritative zone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbdns-log-report
.B --zones
.I file
.B --date
.I YYYY-MM-DD
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rgbdns-log-report
reads original-compatible tinydns request records from standard input. It
counts accepted queries for each configured authoritative zone and distinct
client addresses, including queries below the zone apex. Output is sorted by
total queries in descending order.
.PP
The unique count represents querying client or recursive-resolver IP
addresses. It does not represent unique people or HTTP pageviews.
.PP
The packaged
.B rgbdns-query-report.timer
runs shortly after midnight, reads the preceding local calendar day from the
systemd journal, and submits a plain-text report through a sendmail-compatible
mail transport. Configure
.I /etc/rgbdns/query-report.env
and enable the timer explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --zones " file"
Read one authoritative zone per line. Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.
.TP
.BI --date " YYYY-MM-DD"
Label the report with this date.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rgbdns/query-report.env
Mail recipient, sender, and sendmail path.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns/data
Primary zone source used by the packaged report helper.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns/zones
Secondary zone list used by the packaged report helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tinydns (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR sendmail (1)
